 ## Known differences
 
+### Local durable comparison branch (2026-10-10)
+
+This local-only branch adds opt-in `CAMPFIRE_DURABLE_JOBS=1` transactional SQLite outboxes for model events, persisted retries, and retained job/recipient completion receipts. It changes the upstream best-effort memory-queue contract. `CAMPFIRE_SQLITE_SYNCHRONOUS=FULL` makes all comparison connections sync WAL commits; NORMAL remains the upstream default. The comparison always selects FULL. Jobs remain in the database through shutdown/crash and retry failures with bounded backoff; after ten attempts a failed row is retained for inspection, not silently discarded. A single running application owns each database and resets outstanding leases on restart. Completed audit rows are retained and will grow until explicitly pruned.
+
+The accompanying Mojo repository's `tests/durable_comparison.py` and `bench/durable.py` verify acknowledged message IDs, exact notification recipient receipt sets, queue drain and process-crash recovery. Posting rate includes completion time. Three guarded-out subscription endpoints per posted message are used in the timed workload; real external push delivery is a separate acceptance test. These statistics describe locally modified applications, not untouched upstream releases or a pure language microbenchmark. Media/analysis jobs outside the measured text-post workload are not covered by this comparison's completion claim.
+
+`CAMPFIRE_JOBS_PAUSED=1` keeps workers paused for a controlled restart test without losing outbox work. Normal application tests run in the upstream mode; the shared durability gate runs explicitly in the new mode. The original shared benchmark fixture is copied, never modified.
+
+Rust durable mode also runs database callbacks for index/unread/outbox changes before the message commit and awaits push transport results directly, bypassing the nested in-memory delivery pool.
+
+
 The app keeps the Rails database, storage and current cookie formats compatible. Deliberate
 behavior changes and compatibility limits are listed below.
 
